    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org/",
      "@type": "Recipe",
      "name": "Roasted Vegetable Pasta",
      "description": "Dig into a bowl of Roasted Vegetable Pasta, with garden-fresh veggies caramelized to sweet perfection. Tossed with olive oil, garlic, and herbs, this fast, flavorful dish tastes like late summer in every bite.",
      "author": {
        "@type": "Person",
        "name": "Tonia Schemmel | Feasting at Home"
      },
      "keywords": "vegetable pasta, veggie pasta, roasted vegetable pasta, roasted vegetable pasta recipe, pasta and vegetables, pasta with veggies, veggie pasta recipe,",
      "image": [
        "https://www.feastingathome.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Veggie-Pasta-4-225x225.jpg",
        "https://www.feastingathome.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Veggie-Pasta-4-260x195.jpg",
        "https://www.feastingathome.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Veggie-Pasta-4-320x180.jpg",
        "https://www.feastingathome.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Veggie-Pasta-4.jpg"
      ],
      "url": "https://www.feastingathome.com/roasted-vegetable-pasta/",
      "recipeIngredient": [
        "1 pound zucchini &#8211; about 2 medium zucchini cut in 1/2 moon slices",
        "1 red bell pepper, chopped in one inch bite-sized pieces",
        "8 ounces cremini mushrooms, cut in half or quarter depending on size ",
        "1 red onion, sliced in 1/4 inch wedges",
        "1 pint cherry tomatoes",
        "4 tablespoons olive oil, divided",
        "2 teaspoons Italian seasoning, divided",
        "8 ounces dry pasta (we used rigatoni)",
        "1/4- 1/2 teaspoon red pepper flakes",
        "6 cloves garlic, chopped fine or grated (1/4-1/3 cup)",
        "1 tablespoon fresh rosemary, finely chopped (Optional)",
        "1 lemon zested and juiced",
        "salt to taste",
        "black pepper to taste",
        "1/2 cup fresh basil leaves torn",
        "1/2 cup pecorino cheese or parmesan cheese, grated "
      ],
      "recipeInstructions": [
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Preheat oven to 425°F.",
          "url": "https://www.feastingathome.com/roasted-vegetable-pasta/#instruction-step-1"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Chop zucchini, bell peppers, mushrooms, onion. Place zucchini and bell peppers in a bowl and toss with a few teaspoons of olive oil, salt, pepper, and 1 teaspoon of Italian seasoning. Spread onto a baking sheet- the more room the better they will roast, if too crowded the veggies will steam rather than caramelize. Do the same with the mushrooms, red onion, and cherry tomatoes: place in a bowl, toss with a tablespoon of olive oil, salt, pepper and 1 teaspoon Italian seasoning and spread onto another baking sheet. ",
          "name": "Prep",
          "url": "https://www.feastingathome.com/roasted-vegetable-pasta/#instruction-step-2"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Roast the veggies in the oven for 20-25 minutes, until tender and slightly caramelized. The zucchini tray is usually done in 20 minutes. ",
          "name": "Bake",
          "url": "https://www.feastingathome.com/roasted-vegetable-pasta/#instruction-step-3"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": ". Cook pasta in a large pot of salted water (important for flavor) to al dente while veggies are roasting. Drain and save 1 cup of hot pasta water. ",
          "name": "Pasta",
          "url": "https://www.feastingathome.com/roasted-vegetable-pasta/#instruction-step-4"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": ". In a saute pan, add remaining olive oil (or use 1/2 butter), sauté red pepper flakes and garlic, turn heat to medium low, add rosemary. Let the garlic soften and cook through, stirring all the while- if it is starting to get golden before it cooks through, add a little pasta water.",
          "name": "Saute",
          "url": "https://www.feastingathome.com/roasted-vegetable-pasta/#instruction-step-5"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Add cooked pasta to the pan and toss. To loosen, add a little hot pasta water if desired. Add lemon zest, salt and pepper to taste. Toss in the roasted veggies.  *Adjust flavor again as needed, with more salt, pepper, lemon juice, pasta water, or a drizzle of olive oil.",
          "name": "Combine",
          "url": "https://www.feastingathome.com/roasted-vegetable-pasta/#instruction-step-6"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Top with pecorino cheese, basil, and optional pine nuts.",
          "name": "Garnish",
          "url": "https://www.feastingathome.com/roasted-vegetable-pasta/#instruction-step-7"
        }
      ],
